    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "God’s Case against Jacob’s Heirs"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Ephraim chases the wind",
          "and pursues the east wind.",
          "He continually multiplies lies and violence.",
          "He makes a covenant with Assyria,",
          "and olive oil is carried to Egypt."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord also has a dispute with Judah.",
          "He is about to punish Jacob according to his conduct;",
          "he will repay him based on his actions."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "In the womb he grasped his brother’s heel,",
          "and as an adult he wrestled with God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Jacob struggled with the angel and prevailed;",
          "he wept and sought his favor.",
          "He found him at Bethel,",
          "and there he spoke with him. ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord is the God of Armies;",
          "the Lord is his name."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But you must return to your God.",
          "Maintain love and justice,",
          "and always put your hope in God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A merchant loves to extort",
          "with dishonest scales in his hands."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But Ephraim thinks,",
          "“How rich I have become;",
          "I made it all myself.",
          "In all my earnings,",
          "no one can find any iniquity in me",
          "that I can be punished for! ”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Judgment on Apostate Israel"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I have been the Lord your God",
          "ever since the land of Egypt.",
          "I will make you live in tents again,",
          "as in the festival days."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I will speak through the prophets",
          "and grant many visions;",
          "I will give parables through the prophets."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Since Gilead is full of evil,",
          "they will certainly come to nothing.",
          "They sacrifice bulls in Gilgal;",
          "even their altars will be like piles of rocks",
          "on the furrows of a field."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Further Indictment of Jacob’s Heirs"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Jacob fled to the territory of Aram.",
          "Israel worked to earn a wife;",
          "he tended flocks for a wife."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord brought Israel from Egypt by a prophet,",
          "and Israel was tended by a prophet."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Ephraim has provoked bitter anger,",
          "so his Lord will leave his bloodguilt on him",
          "and repay him for his contempt."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      }
    ]
  },
